  <h3 id="t1">1. Acceptance of these Terms</h3>
  <p>These Terms of Service ("Terms") are an agreement between you and Danthevetinarian ("we," "us," or "our") and govern your use of the Zoo Questy application and related services (the "App"). By downloading, creating an account in, or using the App, you agree to these Terms and to our <a href="#privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. If you do not agree, do not use the App.</p>
  <p><strong>Eligibility and minors.</strong> You must be at least 13 years old to create an account on your own. A child under 13 may use the App only through an account created or approved by a parent or legal guardian, as described in the <a href="#p6">Children's Privacy</a> section of our Privacy Policy. If you are under 18, or under the age of majority where you live, you may use the App only with the involvement and consent of a parent or legal guardian who agrees to these Terms on your behalf. Parents and guardians are responsible for their children's use of the App, including all activity under any account they create or allow a child to use.</p>
  <p><strong>App stores.</strong> If you downloaded the App from the Apple App Store or Google Play, your use is also subject to that store's terms. The store provider is not responsible for the App or its support.</p>

  <h3 id="t2">2. What the App does</h3>
  <p>Zoo Questy is an interactive scavenger hunt for visitors to Omaha's Henry Doorly Zoo and Aquarium (the "Zoo"). Features may include:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Challenges and clues</strong> tied to exhibits and places around the Zoo, which you complete by scanning plaques, matching photos, or solving clues.</li>
    <li><strong>Animal information</strong> about species and exhibits.</li>
    <li><strong>Plaque scanning</strong> to read or verify exhibit signs with your camera.</li>
    <li><strong>Photo matching</strong> challenges that ask you to photograph an animal, exhibit, or landmark.</li>
    <li><strong>Audio stories</strong> about animals and exhibits.</li>
    <li><strong>Quizzes</strong> that test what you have learned.</li>
    <li><strong>Badges and adventure points</strong> earned by completing activities.</li>
    <li><strong>Hide and Seek</strong>, a game mode for finding animals or items around the Zoo.</li>
    <li><strong>"My Zoo,"</strong> a virtual builder where you arrange animals, habitats, and items you have unlocked.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The App is an informal entertainment and educational experience. It does not replace Zoo signage, maps, staff instructions, or official Zoo communications. The App does not include admission to the Zoo; you must have valid admission to take part in on-site challenges.</p>
  <p><strong>Relationship with the Zoo.</strong> The App is operated by Danthevetinarian and is not owned, operated, sponsored, or endorsed by Omaha's Henry Doorly Zoo and Aquarium. The Zoo's name is used only to identify the location where the App is played. All Zoo names and marks belong to their respective owners.</p>

  <h3 id="t3">3. Accounts</h3>
  <p><strong>Sign-up.</strong> Some features require an account. You can sign up with an email address and password, or by signing in with Google or Apple. You agree to provide accurate information and keep it up to date. Choose a display name that is not offensive, misleading, or someone else's name or trademark. Children should not use their full real name as a display name.</p>
  <p><strong>Login and security.</strong> You are responsible for keeping your password confidential and for all activity under your account. Do not share your account or use another person's account. Tell us right away at <a href="mailto:drdanannin2011@gmail.com">drdanannin2011@gmail.com</a> if you believe your account has been accessed without permission.</p>
  <p><strong>Password reset.</strong> If you sign up with email and forget your password, you can request a reset through the App. We will send reset instructions to the email address on your account. If you sign in with Google or Apple, your password is managed by that provider. We will never ask for your password by email, text, or phone.</p>
  <p><strong>Account expectations.</strong> Each account is for one person or one family group, as permitted in the App. You may not create accounts by automated means, create multiple accounts to gain extra points or rewards, or sell, transfer, or rent your account.</p>
  <p><strong>Suspension and termination.</strong> We may suspend, restrict, or terminate your account or access to the App, with or without notice, if we reasonably believe you have violated these Terms, created risk or harm for other users, animals, staff, or us, or if required by law. You may stop using the App and request deletion of your account at any time through the App or by emailing <a href="mailto:drdanannin2011@gmail.com">drdanannin2011@gmail.com</a>. When an account ends, your progress, badges, points, and My Zoo layouts may be permanently lost. Sections that by their nature should survive termination will survive.</p>

  <h3 id="t4">4. Camera and photos</h3>
  <p><strong>When the camera is used.</strong> The App asks for camera access only to support features you choose, such as plaque scanning and photo matching challenges. You can deny or revoke camera access in your device or browser settings at any time, but those features will not work without it.</p>
  <p><strong>How verification works.</strong> When you scan a plaque or submit a photo for a challenge, the App checks the image against what the challenge expects (for example, plaque text or features of an exhibit) to decide whether the challenge is complete. This check may be performed by our service providers on our behalf. Once the check is done, the image is discarded; we do not keep your challenge photos or plaque scans. Verification is not perfect. A valid photo may be rejected or an invalid one accepted, and our decision on whether a challenge is complete is final. Retaking a photo or trying another challenge is usually the fix.</p>
  <p><strong>Appropriate use.</strong> When using the camera, you agree to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Photograph only the animals, exhibits, plaques, and landmarks needed for the challenge.</li>
    <li>Avoid photographing other visitors, especially children, and keep other people's faces out of challenge photos where you can.</li>
    <li>Follow all Zoo photography rules, including any no-photo or no-flash areas.</li>
    <li>Never use flash, tap on glass, lean over barriers, or disturb animals to get a photo.</li>
    <li>Not submit photos that are sexual, violent, hateful, or otherwise inappropriate, or that you do not have the right to share.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We may suspend accounts that break these rules.</p>

  <h3 id="t5">5. Location and real-world safety</h3>
  <p><strong>Device location.</strong> The App does not access or track your device's location (such as GPS). Challenges tied to places in the Zoo are completed by scanning plaques, matching photos, or solving clues, not by detecting where you are. Any map or directions in the App are general guides and may not reflect current paths, closures, or construction.</p>
  <p><strong>Your safety comes first.</strong> The App is a game played in a real, busy place with live animals. When using it, you agree to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Follow all posted Zoo rules, signs, and instructions from Zoo staff and security at all times. Zoo rules and staff instructions always take priority over anything the App says.</li>
    <li>Stay on public paths and in areas open to visitors. Never enter closed, restricted, staff-only, or animal areas, or climb or reach over fences, railings, or barriers, to complete a challenge.</li>
    <li>Pay attention to your surroundings. Do not walk while looking at your screen, and watch for other guests, strollers, wheelchairs, trams, service vehicles, and stairs.</li>
    <li>Supervise children at all times. Adults are responsible for the children in their group and should not let children wander off to complete challenges.</li>
    <li>Never feed, touch, call to, tap glass near, or otherwise disturb animals.</li>
    <li>Take care in weather, heat, and crowds, and stop playing if you feel unwell or unsafe.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>No challenge, clue, or reward requires you to break a Zoo rule or take a risk. If any part of the App seems to suggest otherwise, ignore it and report it to us. You use the App at your own risk and are responsible for your own conduct while playing.</p>

  <h3 id="t6">6. Game progress and virtual items</h3>
  <p><strong>Progress, badges, and points.</strong> You earn badges, adventure points, and other progress by completing challenges, quizzes, scans, and games. Badges, points, unlocked animals and items, and My Zoo layouts (together, "Virtual Items") have no cash value. They cannot be sold, traded, transferred between accounts, or exchanged for money, Zoo admission, or goods unless we expressly offer that in the App.</p>
  <p><strong>License, not ownership.</strong> Virtual Items are licensed to you for personal, non-commercial use within the App. You do not own them, and this license ends when your account ends.</p>
  <p><strong>My Zoo layouts.</strong> Layouts you build in My Zoo are saved to your account. We may limit layout size, available items, or how layouts are displayed.</p>
  <p><strong>Daily and rotating challenges.</strong> Some challenges are available only on certain days, times, or seasons, or only while an exhibit is open. They may rotate, expire, or be replaced without notice. Missing a time-limited challenge does not entitle you to make it up later.</p>
  <p><strong>Changes and resets.</strong> We may adjust, rebalance, rename, or remove badges, point values, challenges, items, and features, including to fix errors, respond to exhibit changes, or prevent cheating. We may correct or reset progress that was earned through a bug, error, or a violation of these Terms. Progress may also be lost through technical failure. We will try to give notice before any planned reset that affects all users, but we cannot guarantee that progress will be preserved.</p>
  <p><strong>Purchases.</strong> The App is free and does not currently offer paid purchases. If we offer in-app purchases in the future, we will update these Terms first. Purchases made through the Apple App Store or Google Play will be governed by that store's payment and refund terms.</p>

  <h3 id="t7">7. User conduct and content</h3>
  <p><strong>Your content.</strong> "User Content" means anything you submit through the App, including display names, photos and scans submitted for verification, animal reports, quiz and feedback responses, and My Zoo layouts. You keep any ownership rights you have in your User Content. You grant us a non-exclusive, royalty-free license to use, store, process, and display your User Content only as needed to operate, verify, moderate, improve, and protect the App. Challenge photos and plaque scans are used only for verification and are discarded afterward, as described in Section 4.</p>
  <p><strong>Your promises about content.</strong> You confirm that you have the right to submit your User Content and that it does not violate anyone's rights or any law.</p>
  <p><strong>Conduct rules.</strong> You agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Submit false, misleading, or joke animal reports, or report an animal missing to cause confusion or alarm.</li>
    <li>Submit photos or other content that is unlawful, sexual, violent, hateful, harassing, or that shows other people without permission.</li>
    <li>Cheat, including submitting photos taken elsewhere or copied from the internet, sharing answers to manipulate scores, or using bots, scripts, or modified versions of the App.</li>
    <li>Harass, threaten, or impersonate other users, Zoo staff, or us.</li>
    <li>Interfere with the App, probe or bypass its security, or reverse engineer it except where the law allows.</li>
    <li>Use the App for any commercial purpose, advertising, or data collection without our written permission.</li>
    <li>Use the App in a way that disturbs animals, other visitors, or Zoo operations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><strong>Moderation.</strong> We may review, refuse, edit, or remove any User Content, and take action on accounts, at our discretion. We are not obligated to monitor User Content, but we may do so.</p>

  <h3 id="t8">8. Animal reports</h3>
  <p>The App lets you report that an animal appears to be missing from, or not visible at, its listed exhibit. Here is how reports work:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Reviewed by our team.</strong> Reports go to the Zoo Questy team, not to Zoo animal care staff or security. We review reports to keep in-app information current. We may not act on every report, and we may not respond to you individually.</li>
    <li><strong>What confirmation may do.</strong> If we confirm a report, we may update the App to show the animal at a different location, mark it as "off exhibit," or temporarily disable related challenges.</li>
    <li><strong>Not an official statement.</strong> A report, and any in-app status that results from one, is not an official statement from the Zoo about any animal's location, health, or status. Animals are often out of view for normal reasons, such as resting, receiving care, or using indoor or off-exhibit areas.</li>
    <li><strong>Emergencies.</strong> Do not use the App to report emergencies. If you see an animal outside its enclosure, an injured animal or person, or any other urgent safety issue, tell the nearest Zoo staff member immediately or call 911.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>False or bad-faith reports violate these Terms.</p>

