  <h3 id="p1">1. Who we are</h3>
  <p>Zoo Questy (the "App") is operated by Danthevetinarian ("we," "us," or "our"). This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect when you use the App, how we use and share it, and the choices you have. The App is not operated by Omaha's Henry Doorly Zoo and Aquarium, and we do not share your information with the Zoo.</p>

  <h3 id="p2">2. Information we collect</h3>
  <p><strong>Account information.</strong> When you create an account, we collect your email address, the display name you choose, and your password (which is stored in protected form, not as plain text). If you sign in with Google or Apple, we receive basic profile information from that provider, such as your name and email address. If you use Apple's "Hide My Email" option, we receive a relay address instead of your real email.</p>
  <p><strong>Game activity.</strong> We store information about how you play so your progress is saved, including challenges completed, quiz answers, badges, adventure points, Hide and Seek results, and your My Zoo layouts.</p>
  <p><strong>Animal reports and messages.</strong> If you report a missing animal or contact us, we collect what you send, such as the exhibit or animal involved, any description you include, and your email address if you write to us.</p>
  <p><strong>Photos and plaque scans.</strong> When you use the camera for a challenge, the image is processed only to check whether the challenge is complete. The image is then discarded. We do not keep challenge photos or plaque scans, add them to your account, or use them to identify people.</p>
  <p><strong>Device and usage information.</strong> Like most apps, the App automatically collects some technical information when you use it, such as your device and browser type, operating system, IP address, pages and features used, the date and time of your visits, and error logs. An approximate region (such as city or state) may be inferred from your IP address. This information is collected through the analytics and visitor-tracking tools built into the platform the App runs on (see Section 7).</p>

  <h3 id="p3">3. Information we do not collect</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>We do not access or track your device's precise location (GPS).</li>
    <li>We do not keep the photos or plaque scans you submit for challenges.</li>
    <li>We do not access your contacts, photo library, or microphone.</li>
    <li>We do not collect payment information, because the App has no paid purchases.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 id="p4">4. How we use information</h3>
  <p>We use the information we collect to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Create and manage your account, including sign-in and password resets.</li>
    <li>Run the game, verify challenges, and save your progress, badges, points, and My Zoo layouts.</li>
    <li>Review animal reports and keep exhibit information in the App up to date.</li>
    <li>Respond to your questions and support requests.</li>
    <li>Understand how the App is used, fix bugs, and improve features.</li>
    <li>Keep the App safe, prevent cheating and abuse, and enforce our Terms of Service.</li>
    <li>Comply with legal obligations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell your personal information, and we do not use it for targeted advertising. The App does not show ads.</p>

  <h3 id="p5">5. How we share information</h3>
  <p>We share information only as described here:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Service providers.</strong> The App is built on and hosted by Base44, which provides our hosting, database, sign-in, image processing for challenge verification, and analytics. Other providers may help us send account emails. These providers process information on our behalf to run the App and are not permitted to use it for their own purposes, except as described in their own privacy terms for the services they provide.</li>
    <li><strong>Sign-in providers.</strong> If you choose to sign in with Google or Apple, that provider processes your sign-in under its own privacy policy.</li>
    <li><strong>Legal and safety reasons.</strong> We may disclose information if required by law, or if we believe in good faith that it is needed to protect the safety of any person, animal, or the App, or to investigate fraud or misuse.</li>
    <li><strong>Business changes.</strong> If the App is sold, merged, or transferred, information may be transferred as part of that transaction, subject to this Policy.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not share information with Omaha's Henry Doorly Zoo and Aquarium, advertisers, or data brokers.</p>

  <h3 id="p6">6. Children's privacy</h3>
  <p>Zoo Questy is designed for families, and we take children's privacy seriously.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Parental consent.</strong> Children under 13 may use the App only through an account created or approved by a parent or legal guardian. We do not knowingly collect personal information from a child under 13 without a parent's or guardian's consent.</li>
    <li><strong>What we collect from children.</strong> We collect only what is needed to run the game: the account details the parent provides, a display name, and game activity such as progress, badges, points, and My Zoo layouts, plus the technical information described in Section 2. Challenge photos are discarded after verification. We do not collect a child's location and do not ask children for more information than the activity needs.</li>
    <li><strong>How it is used and shared.</strong> Children's information is used only to run the App and is shared only with the service providers that help us operate it. We never sell children's information or use it for advertising.</li>
    <li><strong>Display names.</strong> Children should use a nickname, not their real name, as a display name.</li>
    <li><strong>Parents' rights.</strong> A parent or guardian may at any time ask to review the personal information we hold about their child, have it deleted, or refuse further collection or use of it, by emailing <a href="mailto:drdanannin2011@gmail.com">drdanannin2011@gmail.com</a>. We may need to verify that you are the child's parent or guardian before acting on a request. Deleting a child's information will also delete their account and progress.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If we learn that we have collected personal information from a child under 13 without parental consent, we will delete it promptly. If you believe this has happened, please contact us.</p>

  <h3 id="p7">7. Cookies and analytics</h3>
  <p>The App uses cookies, local storage, and similar technologies to keep you signed in, remember your settings, and measure how the App is used. The platform the App runs on, Base44, provides built-in analytics and visitor tracking that record information such as pages viewed, features used, device type, and approximate region. We use this information only to understand and improve the App. You can clear or block cookies in your browser settings, but parts of the App, such as staying signed in, may not work without them.</p>

  <h3 id="p8">8. How long we keep information</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Challenge photos and plaque scans</strong> are discarded once verification is complete.</li>
    <li><strong>Account information and game activity</strong> are kept while your account is active. When you or your parent or guardian ask us to delete the account, we will delete this information within 30 days, except where we must keep some information to comply with law, resolve disputes, or prevent abuse.</li>
    <li><strong>Animal reports and support messages</strong> are kept only as long as needed to handle them and keep the App accurate.</li>
    <li><strong>Analytics and technical logs</strong> are kept for limited periods set by our platform provider.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 id="p9">9. Security</h3>
  <p>We use reasonable measures, including those provided by our hosting platform, to protect your information from loss, misuse, and unauthorized access. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security. Please use a strong password and keep it private.</p>

  <h3 id="p10">10. Your choices and rights</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Access and correction.</strong> You can view and update your account details in the App, or ask us for a copy of the personal information we hold about you.</li>
    <li><strong>Deletion.</strong> You can delete your account through the App or by emailing <a href="mailto:drdanannin2011@gmail.com">drdanannin2011@gmail.com</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Camera access.</strong> You can turn off camera access in your device or browser settings at any time; photo and plaque challenges will not work without it.</li>
    <li><strong>Emails.</strong> We send only account-related emails, such as password resets and important notices about the App or these policies.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Depending on where you live, you may have additional privacy rights under state law. To make any request, email us. We will respond within the time required by applicable law and will not discriminate against you for exercising your rights. The App is operated in the United States, and information is stored and processed in the United States.</p>

  <h3 id="p11">11. Changes to this Policy</h3>
  <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will change the Effective Date above and, for material changes, notify you in the App or by email before they take effect. If a change would affect information we have collected from children, we will seek any new parental consent the law requires.</p>

  <h3 id="p12">12. Contact us</h3>
  <p>For questions about this Privacy Policy or to make a privacy request, contact Danthevetinarian at <a href="mailto:drdanannin2011@gmail.com">drdanannin2011@gmail.com</a>.</p>
